# How the tables are held (decision/002-generated-tables-are-ascii-text-constants): top-level ASCII text constants under
# 512 bytes, fixed-width records, binary search on position. A table is the code points 0 to 10FFFF cut into runs of
# equal value, one record per run: the run's first code point (6 hex digits), then its value. A lookup is the last record
# whose start is at most the code point. A mapping is 6 hex digits per code point in the pool, addressed by 5 hex digits of
# offset (in code points) and 2 of length.
# 
# idna    14 wide: start, the status code (one digit, 0 valid, 1 mapped, 2 deviation, 3 ignored, 4 disallowed, 5 disallowed_std3_valid, 6 disallowed_std3_mapped), a pool field
